      "author": "theadamdanielsson",
      "description": "Grill 2.0 turns your link graph and your answer history into a real tutor, not just a question generator.\n\n- **It reacts when you miss something.** Get a question wrong and Grill routes you to a weak note it builds on (via your `[[wikilinks]]`), quizzes you on that foundation, tells you why, then returns to where you were. Bounded per session.\n- **Mastery is harder to fake.** One lucky answer no longer marks a concept known — Grill waits for a second, corroborating recall. (Notes will read \"known\" more slowly than before, on purpose.)\n- **Weak questions get dropped before you see them.** A deterministic check throws out yes/no stems, multiple-choice stems with no options, answer-leaking hints, near-duplicates, and questions ungrounded in your note — no extra model call. Matters most on small local models.\n- **New notes start at the right level** when their prerequisites are already mastered.\n- **A persona you can rewrite** in `Grill/Instructions.md` (voice only; scoring stays fixed).\n- **Local models are ~24× faster** — thinking mode is now off for Qwen and friends.\n- **Optional confidence check** with an over/underconfidence readout in the debrief (off by default).\n- **A model guide** at `docs/models.md`, by budget and by machine memory.\n\nSee the full changelog in the repo.\n",
